function solve(matrix) {
  const n = matrix.length;
  const result = Array.from({ length: n }, () => new Array(n));

  for (let row = 0; row < n; row++) {
    for (let col = 0; col < n; col++) {
      result[col][n - 1 - row] = matrix[row][col];
    }
  }

  return result;
}
```

Each cell moves to its 90-degree clockwise position without modifying the input. Empty and single-cell matrices are handled naturally. Time: O(n²); space: O(n²) for the returned matrix.

