Sweep through sorted events, processing ends before starts at equal times so rooms can be reused. Skip empty intervals [t,t); the maximum active count is the minimum rooms required.

```javascript
function solve(intervals) {
  const events = [];

  for (const [start, end] of intervals) {
    if (start === end) continue;
    events.push([start, 1], [end, -1]);
  }

  events.sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0] || a[1] - b[1]);

  let active = 0;
  let rooms = 0;

  for (const [, change] of events) {
    active += change;
    rooms = Math.max(rooms, active);
  }

  return rooms;
}
```

Time: O(n log n). Auxiliary space: O(n). Call solve(intervals) directly with valid half-open intervals; the input is not modified.

